## Lore

The Infantry Grunt is the standard foot soldier of a Tech-City army, much
like the Coalition''s Grunt. City infantry are well armed, well trained and
steady, and believe in their role as protectors of what they hold to be the
last bastion of civilization in Australia. As people they differ; as a unit
they exist to preserve the city-state against the chaos outside its walls.
This is the most basic soldier of the Armed Forces.

## GM Notes

The Military O.C.C.s introduction on printed 121 says City troops are less
seasoned than those of the Coalition, Triax or Russia: the average infantry
soldier is 2nd or 3rd level and only 20% are 4th to 8th. The City list on
printed 105 says a City character met outside the walls is an agent, an
exile, a criminal, a rebel or a truant, unless the whole group is a City team
on assignment. Printed 122 says the basic military O.C.C.s of Coalition War
Campaign, Coalition Navy and Triax and the NGR can be adapted for Australia.

Spoken English is 86% plus 3D4%, rolled once; the sheet shows 86.

Kit beyond what the sheet lists (printed 123): a jacket, a full brimmed hat,
a baseball cap, a web belt, a radio communicator with a 5 mile (8 km) range,
a bedroll, an entrenching tool, and six reloads for the weapons. The
Melbourne Army dresses in tan and grey, the Perth Army in dark green and
khaki.

Pay: $1500 a month, +$100 per level of experience, with military room and
board, paid medical treatment and access to military facilities. Quarters are
a dormitory at the city barracks shared with 8-16 other soldiers, depending
on rank; officers get a small apartment.
', 'published', 'data-script'
